---
title: 'Data Selection'
description: 'Enable click-to-select and drag-to-select on $framework charts so users can pick out individual datums or a region of points.'
enterprise: true
---

Data Selection lets users click or drag on the chart to mark individual datums as selected. Selected datums receive a distinct visual treatment and can be read back, set, or cleared programmatically.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Data Selection" name="selection-basic" type="generated" /%}

To enable this feature, set `selection.enabled` to `true`.

```js format="snippet"
{
    selection: {
        enabled: true,
    },
}
```

In the example above, click any bar to toggle its selection. Click an empty area of the chart to clear the selection.

## Click Modes

The `clickMode` option controls how new clicks combine with the existing selection.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Click Modes" name="click-modes" type="generated" /%}

```js format="snippet"
{
    selection: {
        enabled: true,
        clickMode: 'single',
    },
}
```

-   `'single'` (default) replaces the current selection with the clicked datum. Holding {% kbd "Ctrl" /%} or {% kbd "Cmd" /%} during the click temporarily promotes the click to `'multiple'`.
-   `'multiple'` toggles the clicked datum in or out of the existing selection.

Set `enableClickAwayToClear` to `false` to keep the selection in place when the user clicks an empty area of the chart.

## Drag-to-Select

Set `enableDrag` to `true` to let the user draw a rectangle across the chart and select every datum the rectangle covers.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Drag Selection" name="drag-selection" type="generated" /%}

```js format="snippet"
{
    selection: {
        enabled: true,
        enableDrag: true,
        containment: 'any',
    },
}
```

The `containment` option controls which datums the drag rectangle picks up:

-   `'any'` (default) selects a datum if any part of it overlaps the drag rectangle.
-   `'all'` selects a datum only when it is entirely enclosed by the drag rectangle.

## Styling Selected and Unselected Items

When data selection is active, the chart applies a default visual treatment that distinguishes selected datums from unselected ones. Override the styling per series with `series.selection.selectedItem` and `series.selection.unselectedItem`.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Selection Styling" name="selection-styling" type="generated" /%}

```js format="snippet"
{
    series: [
        {
            type: 'bar',
            xKey: 'quarter',
            yKey: 'revenue',
            selection: {
                selectedItem: {
                    fill: '#0b8043',
                    stroke: '#054d27',
                    strokeWidth: 2,
                },
                unselectedItem: {
                    fillOpacity: 0.25,
                },
            },
        },
    ],
}
```

For dynamic per-datum styling, use the series item-styler — `params.selectionState` is set to `'none'`, `'selected'`, or `'unselected'` whenever the data selection module is enabled. See [Stylers](./stylers) for the full styler API.

## Per-Series Configuration

Use `series.selection.enabled` to opt individual series in or out, and `series.selection.containment` to override the chart-level drag rule for one series.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Per-Series Selection" name="per-series-selection" type="generated" /%}

```js format="snippet"
{
    selection: {
        enabled: true,
        enableDrag: true,
    },
    series: [
        {
            type: 'bar',
            xKey: 'quarter',
            yKey: 'revenue',
            selection: { enabled: true },
        },
        {
            type: 'line',
            xKey: 'quarter',
            yKey: 'forecast',
            selection: { enabled: false },
        },
    ],
}
```

Pie series omit the per-series `selection` field, but pie sectors still respond to chart-level click and drag selection.

## Reacting to Selection Changes

Listen for `selectionChange` to react when the selection is updated by either user interaction or an API call.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Selection Change Event" name="selection-change-event" type="generated" /%}

```js format="snippet"
{
    listeners: {
        selectionChange: (event) => {
            console.log(event.source, event.added, event.removed);
        },
    },
}
```

The event payload contains:

-   `source` — `'user-interaction'` or `'api-call'`.
-   `added` — datums added to the selection by this change.
-   `removed` — datums removed from the selection by this change.

Call `event.preventDefault()` from inside the listener to veto the change.

## Programmatic Control

The chart instance exposes three methods for reading and writing the current selection state.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Selection API" name="selection-api" type="generated" /%}

```js format="snippet"
{
    // chart instance methods
    // chart.getSelection(): Iterable<AgSelectionItem>
    // chart.setSelection(items: Iterable<AgSelectionItemIds>): void
    // chart.clearSelection(): void
}
```

-   `chart.getSelection()` returns an iterable of every currently selected item, each with `seriesId`, `itemId`, and `datum`.
-   `chart.setSelection(items)` replaces the current selection with the supplied items.
-   `chart.clearSelection()` removes every selected item across all series.

## Compatibility

Data Selection is an enterprise feature and requires `SelectionModule` to be registered. It is not supported on histogram series or on standalone charts.

